## Third-party provenance

The manuals are **distillations written in our own words**, not reproductions.
Several of them distil sources that are not ours to relicense, and the
obligations travel with the material regardless of what this file says:

| Manual | Source | Terms |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 01, 02, 04–09 | Andrew Loomis, *Drawing the Head and Hands* (1956), *Figure Drawing for All It's Worth* (1943), *Creative Illustration* (1947), *Successful Drawing* (1951), *The Eye of the Painter* (1961) | US copyright status contested: widely circulated as public domain on lapsed renewals, and reissued under licence from the estate. Treated as all rights reserved: principles distilled and pages cited; nothing reproduced. |
| 01, 05, 08 | Michael Hampton, *Figure Drawing: Design and Invention* (2009) | All rights reserved. Same handling, cited by section. |
| 03 | Klaus Janson, *The DC Comics Guide to Inking Comics* (2003); Jack Hamm, *Drawing the Head and Figure* (1963) | All rights reserved. Same handling. |
| 06 | Ernest R. Norling, *Perspective Made Easy* (1939; Dover 1999) | All rights reserved. Same handling. |
| 08 | Jack Faragasso, *Mastering Drawing the Human Figure* (1998) | All rights reserved, with a retrieval-system clause: distilled and cited, and its text is kept out of the retrieval corpus. |
| 10, 12 | George Bokhua, *Principles of Logo Design* | All rights reserved. Distilled and cited, never quoted at length. |
| 11 | Robin Williams, *The Non-Designer's Design Book*; Doyald Young, *Fonts and Logos* | All rights reserved. Same handling. |
| 12 §2.5 | *Graphic Design and Print Production Fundamentals* (BCcampus / Graphic Communications Open Textbook Collective) | **CC BY 4.0** — attributed in the manual. §2.4 of that book is CC BY-NC-ND 3.0 and is **not** adapted here. |
| 13 | `EpicInfographics` | MIT. Distilled with attribution. |
| 14 | *Graphic Design and Print Production Fundamentals*, ch. 5 **Pre-press** (§5.2 Raster Image Processing, §5.5 Transparency) | **CC BY 4.0** — attributed in the manual. This chapter carries no "otherwise noted" exception, so unlike §2.4 it is adapted here, with the one short §5.5 sentence quoted and credited. |
| 15 | Deshpande, Trajkova, Knowlton & Magerko, *Observable Creative Sense-Making*, C&C '23 | **CC BY 4.0** — the only adaptable paper in `reference/papers/`. Its newness scale and applicability clause are adapted and attributed. Davis et al., *Creative Sense-Making*, C&C '17 (ACM, all rights reserved) is **cited only**, for the 4:1 coding cost. |
| 16 | — | No external source. Documents a Polson subsystem and the studio's own form-versus-substance policy. |
| 17 | Klaus Janson, *The DC Comics Guide to Pencilling Comics* (Watson-Guptill / DC Comics, 2002), ch. 1 and ch. 13 | All rights reserved. Distilled and cited in our own words, never quoted at length — same handling as the Bokhua row. |
| 18 | Davis, Hsiao, Singh, Lin & Magerko, *Creative Sense-Making*, C&C '17 | ACM, all rights reserved. Its three stated limitations of video coding are cited and answered, not quoted. The OCSM applicability clause (CC BY 4.0) is attributed as in Manual 15. |

Manuals 01–09 once cited John Guy, *Imaginative Drawing* (2025). Every citation was withdrawn on 2026-09-02, because
its terms ask that it be shared only whole and withhold permission for any part of it to be used to train AI. Nothing
of it remains in these manuals, and it is not to be re-added.

`docs/creative-sense-making.md` implements a framework from the research
literature — principally Nicholas Davis's work on creative sense-making and the
CCSM schema, cited in the document itself. Those papers are third-party and
mostly all-rights-reserved; the document distils and cites them and reproduces
none of them. `reference/` is third-party material, is not distributed with this
repository, and is covered by neither licence.

If you adapt a manual, CC BY-SA 4.0 requires you to share alike and to attribute
this project — and it does not relieve you of the obligations in the table above
for whatever those manuals distil.
